ates, the velocity vector is"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.25968,"w":0.43335,"h":0.01432,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Hence, we can express the velocity vector in terms of ur and uu as"},{"x":0.16428,"y":0.27333,"w":0.08345,"h":0.02083,"fs":0.01151,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"v = r# ur + ru"},{"x":0.50468,"y":0.27808,"w":0.07462,"h":0.02126,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"v = r# = d"},{"x":0.56887,"y":0.27808,"w":0.13198,"h":0.02854,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dt(rur) = r# ur + ru#"},{"x":0.70053,"y":0.27808,"w":0.08904,"h":0.02315,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"r = r#ur + ru"},{"x":0.2486,"y":0.28094,"w":0.01784,"h":0.01248,"fs":0.01151,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"uu."},{"x":0.78957,"y":0.28654,"w":0.01985,"h":0.01387,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"uu."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.30958,"w":0.58896,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"See Figure 13.31. As in the previous section, we use Newton’s dot notation for time deriva- tives to keep the formulas as simple as we can: u#"},{"x":0.39202,"y":0.31449,"w":0.55948,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"means du>dt, and so on. The acceleration is"},{"x":0.67561,"y":0.31449,"w":0.11377,"h":0.02474,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r means dur>dt, u"},{"x":0.49713,"y":0.35481,"w":0.13468,"h":0.02315,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"a = v# = (r$ur + r# u#"},{"x":0.63149,"y":0.35481,"w":0.05378,"h":0.02278,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r) + (r#u"},{"x":0.79331,"y":0.35481,"w":0.0091,"h":0.02125,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"u#"},{"x":0.68653,"y":0.36262,"w":0.0534,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"uu + ru"},{"x":0.7406,"y":0.36262,"w":0.05271,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"uu + ru"},{"x":0.8021,"y":0.3633,"w":0.01488,"h":0.01385,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"u)."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.37783,"w":0.28075,"h":0.02127,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"When Equations (2) are used to evaluate u#"},{"x":0.64302,"y":0.37783,"w":0.04768,"h":0.02278,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r and u#"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.38632,"w":0.59305,"h":0.02965,"fs":0.01279,"n":2