,"k":0,"t":"0 r0 = 2r2 + z2."},{"x":0.39203,"y":0.60089,"w":0.50599,"h":0.01432,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The vectors ur, uu, and k make a right-handed frame (Figure 13.32) in which"},{"x":0.4887,"y":0.62326,"w":0.3367,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"ur * uu = k, uu * k = ur, k * ur = uu."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.65917,"w":0.17827,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Planets Move in Planes"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.68381,"w":0.59307,"h":0.04351,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Newton’s law of gravitation says that if r is the radius vector from the center of a sun of mass M to the center of a planet of mass m, then the force F of the gravitational attraction between the planet and sun is"},{"x":0.60285,"y":0.73792,"w":0.08502,"h":0.02007,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"F = - GmM"},{"x":0.65943,"y":0.73816,"w":0.04898,"h":0.02941,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 r0 2 r 0 r0"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.77589,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"(Figure 13.33). The number G is the universal gravitational constant. If we measure mass in kilograms, force in newtons, and distance in meters, G is about 6.6738 * 10-11 Nm2 kg-2."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.79812,"w":0.58891,"h":0.03662,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Combining the gravitation law with Newton’s second law, F = mr$, for the force act- ing on the planet gives"},{"x":0.08803,"y":0.82286,"w":0.01,"h":0.02291,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"r 0 r0"},{"x":0.59545,"y":0.8416,"w":0.09412,"h":0.02126,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"mr$ = - GmM"},{"x":0.66113,"y":0.84303,"w":0.05754,"h":0.02941,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 r0 2 r 0 r0 ,"},{"x":0.12081,"y":0.85514,"w":0.0688,"h":0.01518,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"F = −GmM"},{"x":0.16572,"y":0.85528,"w":0.0384,"h":0.02361,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 r0 2 r 0 r0"},{"x":0.60726,"y":0.88125,"w":0.07048,"h":0.02126,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r$ = - GM"},{"x":0.65521,"y":0.88268,"w":0.05163,"h":0.02941,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 r0 2 r 0 r0 ."},{"x":0.08775,"y":0.89252,"w":0.24739,"h":0.04297,"fs":0.01151,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 13.33 The force of gravity is directed along the line joining the centers of mass."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.92235,"w":0.51461,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The planet is therefore accelerated toward the sun’s center of mass at all times."}]}